\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. Art Thou weary, art thou languid,
\par Art thou sore distressed?
\par Come to Me, saith One, and, coming,
\par                                 Be at rest!
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. Hath He marks to lead me to Him,
\par If He be my guide?
\par In His feet and hands are wound-prints,
\par                                  And His side.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. Hath He diadem as Monarch
\par That His brow adorns?
\par Yea, a crown in every surety,
\par                             But of thorns!
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. If I find Him, if I follow,
\par What His guerdon here?
\par Many a sorrow, many a labour,
\par                         Many a tear.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 5\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 5. If I still hold closely to Him,
\par What hath He at last?
\par Sorrow vanquished, labour ended,
\par                        Jordan past.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 6\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 6. If I ask Him to receive me,
\par Will He say me nay?
\par Not till earth and not till heaven
\par                         Pass away.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 7\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 7. Finding, following, keeping, struggling
\par Is He sure to bless?
\par Saints, apostles, prophets, martyrs,
\par                        Answer: Yes!\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b 
\par }

